cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyTPS in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "PyTPS: an educational radiotherapy treatment planning system"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Radfar
    given-names: Kazim
    affiliation: "Tehran University of Medical Sciences"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   (add your ORCID iD here)
version: "0.2.2"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kazimradfar/PyTPS"
url: "https://github.com/kazimradfar/PyTPS"
abstract: >-
  PyTPS is a free, open-source radiotherapy treatment planning system for teaching medical physics
  students. It covers DICOM CT import, contouring, static fields and VMAT arcs, pencil-beam dose
  calculation, IMRT and VMAT optimisation, DVH evaluation and plan comparison, with a beam's-eye view,
  3D and treatment room views and a guided VMAT-TBI exercise. It is not intended for clinical use.
keywords:
  - radiotherapy
  - treatment planning
  - medical physics
  - education
  - IMRT
  - VMAT
  - total body irradiation
  - dose calculation
